_model: proposition
---
title: Book I, Proposition 4
---
body:

<div class="theorem">
<h1>Proposition 4</h1>

<div class="statement">If two triangles have the two sides equal to two sides respectively, and have the angles contained by the equal straight lines equal, then they also have the base equal to the base, the triangle equals the triangle, and the remaining angles equal the remaining angles respectively, namely those opposite the equal sides.</div>

<p><i>Milestone 1 stub — full conversion deferred.</i></p>

<p>This page exists to confirm the proposition model and template handle multiple pages cleanly. The full propI.4 body (including the side-by-side diagrams that surfaced the superposition / forward-reference bugs earlier) will be ported as part of the full Book I conversion.</p>

<p>Reference: <a href="https://www.euclids-elements.org/elements/bookI/propI4.html">propI.4 on euclids-elements.org</a>.</p>

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
</div>
